# OPUS-ROOT-CALL-20260930-17: the two-argument form written above Other's declaration.  The language (docs :668):
# Model exists, so `Model: Other extra` is Model's call -- an ordinary named Structure takes no argument -- whatever
# Other is.  IMPLEMENTATION DEBT, pinned as such (K03 NS-ROLES-VIS; Codex K03-VIS-CALL-CLASSIFICATION-20261007-16):
# with Other invisible above its definition the translator still takes the old typed receiving route
# (l2_colon_bind_shape, l2_check_bind) and refuses the candidate; the call classification (NS-ROLES-CALL) is next.
Model:
    size_t: value 1U
end: Model

int: extra 1
Model: Other extra

Other:
    size_t: p 2U
end: Other
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 7; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
